VERDICT: FAIL
CHECKER: checker-second
FAMILY: adversarial
TASK: WS3
ATTEMPT: 2
---
Scope reviewed: SPEC.md "### WS3 — A chain step never crashes the projection;
a failed analysis never bricks the page (Tier 3)" acceptance criteria 1-4,
plus dispatch note "Attempt 2 adds engine.GuardrailsGovernStep(s) ... used by
stepper.go, spending_floor.go and monte_carlo.go", plus the attack-surface
list naming "the guardrail chart trigger lines/markers (GuardrailPeak/
Baseline/CutTrigger/RaiseTrigger on year summaries, handlers_guardrail_graph.go,
charts)" explicitly.

== Confirmed working (tried to refute, could not) ==

1. Oracle re-run on my snapshot: ORACLE PASS.
   `bash .swarm/tier3/WS3/accept.sh <snapshot>` -> tail:
   "== all 3 variants passed" / "ORACLE PASS" (all 15 table/D4 checks PASS,
   incl. A->B cuts before/none after, B->A none before/at + acts after,
   D4 full-page render + Remove + re-analysis).

2. `engine.GuardrailsGovernStep` is genuinely the single predicate for the
   engine layer: grep confirms stepper.go, spending_floor.go and
   monte_carlo.go are its only production call sites; no remaining
   `st.Guardrails != nil` or inlined `s.Guardrails != nil && s.Guardrails.Enabled`
   survives in those three files.

3. Mutation-kill checks (own copy, reverted after each):
   - monte_carlo.go: reverting `guardrailsActive := engine.GuardrailsGovernStep(s)`
     to `st.Guardrails != nil` (the exact attempt-1 defect, ruling 2026-09-23d)
     -> `TestMonteCarloAdaptiveSpendingFollowsActiveStepGuardrails` FAILs
     ("depleted at year 3.67, final balance 0" instead of Survives).
   - stepper.go: reverting the activeMultiplier gate from
     `if activeGuardrailsOn && st.Guardrails != nil` to `if st.Guardrails != nil`
     (multiplier/trigger carry-over after an on->off transition) ->
     `TestChainGuardrailsOnToOff` FAILs with a PANIC (nil `s.Guardrails`
     dereferenced computing GuardrailCutTrigger) — the named mutation is
     killed, and killed hard.
   - `go test ./internal/services/retirement/... ./internal/handlers/whatif/...`
     all packages ok (criterion 6).

== Refutation that succeeded: chart-layer split classification ==

`internal/handlers/whatif/handlers.go` was NOT migrated to
`GuardrailsGovernStep` (it is not in the WS3.2 manifest) even though it is a
real per-step consumer of guardrail state, exactly the class this task
exists to eliminate (SPEC.md's own "Why" column for WS3: "money figures
after a transition"; my dispatch's attack-surface list names this file
line-by-line: "handlers_guardrail_graph.go, charts").

`buildProjectionChartData`'s guardrail-line gate (handlers.go:844):
  guardrailsEnabled := settings != nil && settings.Guardrails != nil &&
      settings.Guardrails.Enabled && len(...) > 0
`settings` here is the PRIMARY (pre-chain) step's settings — a single
whole-chart boolean, not `GuardrailsGovernStep` evaluated per year/step.
`buildGuardrailChartSummary` (handlers.go:570) uses the identical
primary-only gate for the "Guardrails: N cuts/raises..." caption under the
chart.

Built the snapshot, served it with the oracle's own harness
(`.swarm/tier3/lib/common.sh`) and the oracle's own a-to-b / b-to-a
fixtures (`make_fixture.py`), and fetched the SAME endpoint the live
projection-chart card on GET /whatif calls (`/whatif/chart/projection`,
routes.go:1277, `web/templates/pages/whatif.html:212`
`{{template "whatif-projection-chart" .}}`).

A -> B (guardrails on -> off at year 13), `curl $WS_BASE/whatif/chart/projection`,
"Cut trigger" trace:
  x = [0..32, 32.25]  (34 points, one per year + end-of-chart)
  y = [...,2160775.41 (year 12), 2160775.41 (year 13), 0, 0, 0, ... 0]  (years 14-33 all 0)
  text[13..] = "Cut if balance ≤ $0.00 at the year 14 check" ... through
  "... at the year 33 check" (20 consecutive false $0.00 labels)
"Raise trigger" trace: identical pattern, "$2,640,000.00" through year 13
then "$0.00" for every year after.
This is a literal false dollar figure rendered on screen: the chart tells
the user "guardrails will cut if your balance falls to $0" for a step that
has NO guardrails at all — not merely stale, but semantically wrong (no such
threshold exists once guardrails stop governing).

B -> A (guardrails off -> on at year 3/4), same probe on
`/whatif/chart/projection`:
  trace names present = ['Portfolio Balance', 'Key events',
  'Guardrail cuts / raises']  — "Cut trigger" and "Raise trigger" are
  ABSENT ENTIRELY from the chart, even though guardrails ARE governing
  spending from year 4 onward (the SAME server's `/whatif/results-full`
  table shows cuts in that range per the oracle's own PASS, and the
  "Guardrail cuts / raises" marker trace on this very chart response is
  non-empty — the event marker layer is correct, only the gate for the
  trigger LINES and the summary caption is wrong). The
  `buildGuardrailChartSummary` caption ("Guardrails: ...") is likewise
  fully suppressed for the entire B->A projection because its gate is also
  `settings.Guardrails.Enabled` on the PRIMARY (B, off) settings — a user
  chaining into a guardrail step gets zero on-chart indication guardrails
  are active later in their own plan.

Confirms this is genuine split classification (recurring defect class 1):
the per-year `YearlySummaries[i].GuardrailCutTrigger/RaiseTrigger` fields
ARE correctly computed by the fixed stepper.go (0 for ungoverned years,
correct positive values for governed years — I read these directly off the
JSON above), but the CHART's decision of "should I even use those numbers /
should I show the trigger line/summary at all" is a second, stale
classifier keyed on the primary settings only, never reconciled with
`GuardrailsGovernStep`. The individual event markers ("Guardrail cuts /
raises", the Guardrail Events card guarded by
`.Analysis.Projection.GuardrailEvents`) are correct in both directions —
only the CutTrigger/RaiseTrigger line traces and the chart caption are
wrong.

This can only be triggered by a guardrail-governing scenario-chain
transition (a non-chained plan either always has guardrailsEnabled=true
with correct, unvarying trigger values for every year, or has it false and
shows nothing) — i.e., it is not a pre-existing, unrelated defect; it is a
second, unmigrated instance of the exact classification bug WS3 was
chartered to eliminate, and it was unreachable/unobservable before this
task's own fix (pre-WS3, this scenario panicked before any chart ever
rendered — SPEC.md "Chain crash (WS3)": "A step whose settings have
Guardrails == nil -> nil deref -> panic"). The fix is straightforward and
within the same file/predicate family the worker already touched this
attempt (`buildProjectionChartData` and `buildGuardrailChartSummary` in
handlers.go should derive per-year/whole-chain guardrail-governance from
the projection's own per-year data — e.g. `GuardrailsGovernStep` evaluated
against the correct step, or simply `ys.GuardrailCutTrigger > 0` — instead
of the primary-only `settings.Guardrails.Enabled` gate).

== Other attack surfaces checked, no defect found ==
- handlers_guardrail_optimizer.go / handlers_spending_optimizer.go: both
  explicitly refuse chained scenarios at the request boundary
  ("Chained scenarios are not supported[ by the guardrail optimizer]." /
  400) before any candidate/graph work runs, so `GuardrailsGovernStep` vs.
  `.Guardrails != nil` divergence cannot occur there (grep + read,
  handlers_guardrail_optimizer.go:99-102, handlers_spending_optimizer.go:
  163-165, 210-212).
- `buildGuardrailAnchors` ("Next yearly check" panel): gated on primary
  settings but only ever describes the immediately-upcoming (year-0) check,
  which is legitimately governed by the primary step in every chain
  (transitions happen later) — correct in both fixtures.
- `handlers_guardrail_graph.go` (optimizer candidate graph preview): only
  reachable after a successful (i.e. non-chained, per the guard above)
  optimizer run — chains never reach it.
- Monte Carlo / lifestyle-outcomes: now correctly keyed on
  `GuardrailsGovernStep`, verified by the mutation-kill above and by
  `TestMonteCarloAdaptiveSpendingFollowsActiveStepGuardrails` passing
  unmutated.
- MCP plan tools (`internal/services/mcpsvc/plan/*.go`): grep for
  "Guardrail" returns nothing — no independent classifier there to
  diverge.
- D4: the underlying nil-deref this task fixes is in the shared engine
  (stepper.go), so every entry point (GET /whatif, results-full, MC) is
  protected by the same fix; `handleWhatIfResultsFull`'s own `renderError`
  fallback is an HTMX partial into an already-rendered page, not a bricked
  full page, and out of D4's stated scope (GET /whatif's inputs column).

== Verdict ==
FAIL. Acceptance criteria 1/2 ("no guardrail multiplier/figure appears
after the transition" / "guardrails can act after the transition") are met
on the Year-by-Year table and event list but NOT on the projection chart —
a second, explicitly-named attack surface for this task — which shows a
fabricated $0.00 guardrail trigger after an on->off transition and shows NO
trigger line or summary at all after an off->on transition despite
guardrails genuinely governing that range. This is the same split-
classification defect class ruling 2026-09-23d already caught once this
attempt (Monte Carlo) in a sibling consumer that was migrated; the chart
consumer was not.
